# following MISRA-C:2012 rules are deviated for it because they are inherent to
# the host-tool role and the Unicorn callback ABI it is built on, not defects:
#   21.6  -- it is a CLI tool; <stdio.h> IS its interface (printf/fopen/...).
#   21.3  -- host tool; malloc/free for framebuffers is appropriate (no P10).
#   11.1/11.2/11.3/11.5/11.8 -- Unicorn's hook/MMIO ABI passes user data as
#            void* and installs handlers via function-pointer casts; both are
#            unavoidable.
